1
00:00:37,016 --> 00:00:38,267
Hey. Kim.

2
00:00:38,351 --> 00:00:39,894
EPISODE 7

3
00:00:39,977 --> 00:00:42,938
Geez. Is this your first day in business?
Don't worry about it.

4
00:00:43,022 --> 00:00:44,774
- Just buy me a drink--
- Hey, boys!

5
00:00:47,109 --> 00:00:48,152
Wait, hold on.

6
00:00:48,861 --> 00:00:50,738
- What the hell?
- I don't have much time.

7
00:00:50,821 --> 00:00:52,782
So I'll keep it short.

8
00:00:52,865 --> 00:00:56,285
There's an important shipment coming in
from China tomorrow night, right?

9
00:00:56,369 --> 00:00:59,205
We need to make some adjustments
to those goods.

10
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:02,958
So, we need to borrow your little shop
for just two days.

11
00:01:03,042 --> 00:01:06,796
Think of it as a location sponsorship.

12
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:08,089
What the hell?

13
00:01:08,172 --> 00:01:12,093
What are these assholes on about?

14
00:01:12,176 --> 00:01:14,428
Hey, what are you doing? Get 'em!

15
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,851
What are you waiting for? Go ahead.

16
00:01:20,935 --> 00:01:22,770
- By myself? What about you?
- You scared?

17
00:01:22,853 --> 00:01:24,522
Scared? Hell no.

18
00:02:18,743 --> 00:02:19,744
I'll kill them.

19
00:02:34,175 --> 00:02:35,176
What the hell?

20
00:02:51,108 --> 00:02:52,109
So what's it going to be?

21
00:02:52,651 --> 00:02:53,652
Can we borrow it?

22
00:02:58,741 --> 00:03:00,826
- Ow, my back.
- Geez, it's so dusty.

23
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,954
You should've helped sooner
instead of trying to look cool.

24
00:03:04,622 --> 00:03:08,334
- There were only like seven guys.
- I had them, but you jumped in.

25
00:03:08,417 --> 00:03:10,169
You would've been dead without me.

26
00:03:10,252 --> 00:03:12,046
You would have been dead
if it weren't for me.

27
00:03:14,048 --> 00:03:16,884
Hey, Seong-won. Location secured.

28
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:19,386
Now let's get set up. Yeah.

29
00:03:21,555 --> 00:03:24,225
- Hey, you're so dusty.
- Stop it!

30
00:03:26,811 --> 00:03:29,146
We'll be working together from now on.

31
00:03:29,230 --> 00:03:30,648
So I'll speak casually.

32
00:03:30,731 --> 00:03:33,818
- Is that okay?
- Yes, whatever works for you.

33
00:03:33,901 --> 00:03:35,194
I like your attitude.

34
00:03:36,111 --> 00:03:37,112
First things first.

35
00:03:37,905 --> 00:03:39,281
I need you to operate this.

36
00:03:41,742 --> 00:03:42,743
This thing?

37
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:45,079
Yeah, why? It's small.
Doesn't look too difficult.

38
00:03:47,748 --> 00:03:50,084
So, what will you be doing
while I'm driving this?

39
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:51,168
Me?

40
00:03:52,127 --> 00:03:53,379
That.

41
00:03:58,926 --> 00:04:00,344
- Start it.
- Okay.

42
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,137
That's it.

43
00:04:02,221 --> 00:04:04,515
Step on the clutch and just push forward.

44
00:04:05,182 --> 00:04:08,394
That's it. Gently. That's it.
It's okay. You're okay.

45
00:04:08,477 --> 00:04:11,146
- Should I go?
- Yes. Step on it a bit.

46
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:13,566
- This thing is so loud.
- No, look over here.

47
00:04:15,067 --> 00:04:16,652
- Isn't this too fast?
- Easy, right?

48
00:04:16,735 --> 00:04:18,863
- Yeah.
- Okay, turn left here.

49
00:04:18,946 --> 00:04:19,947
Left turn?

50
00:04:38,716 --> 00:04:39,717
That's it.

51
00:04:40,509 --> 00:04:41,760
That's it.

52
00:05:07,745 --> 00:05:09,079
Let me touch it.

53
00:05:14,418 --> 00:05:15,419
I'll take this one.

54
00:05:18,088 --> 00:05:19,673
- Which mask do you want?
- What?

55
00:05:20,215 --> 00:05:21,216
I don't want it.

56
00:05:25,262 --> 00:05:28,682
We have to lure them in.
We're going to lead them over here.

57
00:05:28,766 --> 00:05:29,767
Time it perfectly.

58
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:31,977
Counting the guys from China,
there are going to be a lot of them.

59
00:05:32,061 --> 00:05:34,229
What's the most important thing? Timing.

60
00:05:37,149 --> 00:05:38,525
We're all set, right?

61
00:05:38,609 --> 00:05:42,321
- Yes. It's perfect.
- It's been so long since my last bust.

62
00:05:42,404 --> 00:05:44,406
My heart is pounding.

63
00:05:46,116 --> 00:05:49,328
Well, it looks like we're ready,
so let's get something to eat.

64
00:05:49,411 --> 00:05:52,373
- What?
- How can you eat before this?

65
00:05:52,498 --> 00:05:55,834
I'm suggesting it for your sake.
You're so weak that you got beaten up.

66
00:05:56,335 --> 00:05:57,711
I'll make you strong.

67
00:05:59,713 --> 00:06:01,632
- You got money?
- You should pay.

68
00:06:02,216 --> 00:06:03,425
You're the oldest.

69
00:06:04,134 --> 00:06:07,471
KOREAN BEEF

70
00:06:17,272 --> 00:06:18,315
That's delicious.

71
00:06:31,412 --> 00:06:32,830
Slow down a little.

72
00:06:33,497 --> 00:06:34,999
Doesn't your boss buy you meat?

73
00:06:35,124 --> 00:06:37,167
I'm so used to eating
expired store lunch boxes.

74
00:06:37,376 --> 00:06:38,711
I never get to have proper beef.

75
00:06:39,211 --> 00:06:40,212
This is amazing.

76
00:06:40,295 --> 00:06:42,881
Real Korean beef is on another level.

77
00:06:43,590 --> 00:06:44,633
He only fed you expired food?

78
00:06:45,467 --> 00:06:48,637
- What a scumbag boss.
- Who are you calling a scumbag boss?

79
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:50,931
When did I only feed you
expired food, bastard?

80
00:06:51,015 --> 00:06:53,600
Every day.
And only the most unpopular ones.

81
00:06:53,684 --> 00:06:54,977
I fed you other stuff!

82
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:57,229
I know it's a tough world out there.

83
00:06:57,312 --> 00:07:01,233
But how can you not buy this young man
some Korean beef?

84
00:07:01,316 --> 00:07:04,611
Have the bibimbap with the noodles.
It tastes better that way.

85
00:07:04,695 --> 00:07:06,488
- Really? Can I do that?
- Of course.

86
00:07:06,572 --> 00:07:08,323
I'm going to eat till I burst.

87
00:07:08,407 --> 00:07:11,660
You're gonna make people think
I never buy you anything.

88
00:07:11,744 --> 00:07:13,245
Hey, we were busy with the store.

89
00:07:13,328 --> 00:07:16,331
We didn't have time because
it was just the two of us running it.

90
00:07:17,166 --> 00:07:18,709
And besides...

91
00:07:18,792 --> 00:07:20,836
I haven't had much beef in my life either.

92
00:07:22,129 --> 00:07:24,590
But why did you work so hard
at the convenience store?

93
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:29,303
Well, he worked hard,
so I just worked hard too.

94
00:07:29,386 --> 00:07:32,431
- Do you need a reason to work hard?
- You even got an award.

95
00:07:32,514 --> 00:07:34,641
For "Friendly Convenience Store"
or something.

96
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:38,645
Maybe that's a better fit
than being a gangster, huh?

97
00:07:38,729 --> 00:07:40,064
No way.

98
00:07:40,147 --> 00:07:42,691
His calling is being number two
in the Hwasan Sect.

99
00:07:42,775 --> 00:07:45,486
He's just being patient now
to avenge the big boss.

100
00:07:45,569 --> 00:07:47,237
- Isn't that right?
- Something like that.

101
00:07:47,321 --> 00:07:51,366
I can't believe you got an award
for friendliness.

102
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:56,080
Hey, what's wrong with being friendly?
It's not like it's impossible.

103
00:07:56,163 --> 00:07:59,833
This guy lived undercover for ten years.

104
00:08:00,542 --> 00:08:02,544
What are you talking about? Undercover?

105
00:08:02,628 --> 00:08:05,422
Come on, Mr. Jeong. Be honest with us.

106
00:08:06,173 --> 00:08:08,008
Did you marry your wife
because you loved her?

107
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:12,721
I mean, we saw you get married,
and we saw you have a child.

108
00:08:12,805 --> 00:08:13,889
But we couldn't believe it.

109
00:08:13,972 --> 00:08:15,432
Because in movies, right?

110
00:08:15,516 --> 00:08:18,519
Agents get married and
do all sorts of things for their cover.

111
00:08:19,436 --> 00:08:20,521
Huh?

112
00:08:20,938 --> 00:08:22,773
Did you give him an order to get married?

113
00:08:23,524 --> 00:08:26,068
Why would I go as far as
ordering him to marry?

114
00:08:26,151 --> 00:08:28,904
- You watch too many movies.
- No, that's not it.

115
00:08:28,987 --> 00:08:32,074
There's a limit
to how much a man can be whipped.

116
00:08:32,616 --> 00:08:35,077
It's almost impossible to believe
how low he ranks in his family.

117
00:08:35,744 --> 00:08:37,579
- For real?
- So that's the real you?

118
00:08:37,704 --> 00:08:40,207
Hey, what do you people take me for?

119
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:42,417
You got married as a cover
to work at the restaurant, right?

120
00:08:43,752 --> 00:08:45,087
Hey, stop eating!

121
00:08:46,922 --> 00:08:48,382
I'm not buying you food
to take all this crap.

122
00:08:48,465 --> 00:08:49,633
- Stop eating!
- Come on!

123
00:08:49,716 --> 00:08:51,510
- What's with you?
- You only get to eat the sauce!

124
00:08:51,593 --> 00:08:54,179
This is just bad table manners!
We get it already!

125
00:08:55,013 --> 00:08:57,850
It's not even that expensive.
I checked the price on my way in.

126
00:08:57,933 --> 00:09:00,310
Hey, it won't be that much.
Order whatever you want.

127
00:09:00,394 --> 00:09:02,604
Plus, you're not even buying.
He's taking care of it.

128
00:09:02,688 --> 00:09:03,730
- Really?
- Order more!

129
00:09:03,814 --> 00:09:05,649
Ma'am, can we get some more meat?

130
00:09:07,234 --> 00:09:09,611
Wow, look at the quality of this.

131
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:15,993
What are you doing?

132
00:09:23,458 --> 00:09:24,751
I've got a lot on my mind.

133
00:09:27,045 --> 00:09:30,299
Like you said, I've lived as
a convenience store owner for ten years.

134
00:09:31,258 --> 00:09:33,927
I'm worried if I can pull this off.

135
00:09:36,305 --> 00:09:37,431
Getting scared again?

136
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:40,851
Why do you keep saying I'm scared?

137
00:09:40,934 --> 00:09:42,936
You think I'd be scared
of that bastard Yoo In-gu?

138
00:09:43,645 --> 00:09:46,398
It's just that they've got a lot of men.

139
00:09:46,857 --> 00:09:50,110
And I got my ass beaten
because I overestimated myself.

140
00:09:51,528 --> 00:09:53,947
So naturally, I've been having doubts.

141
00:09:54,948 --> 00:09:56,450
Maybe my body can't take this.

142
00:09:58,869 --> 00:10:00,037
What about you?

143
00:10:00,871 --> 00:10:02,372
Aren't you worried?

144
00:10:02,915 --> 00:10:04,124
Is your body

145
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:06,251
like it was ten years ago?

146
00:10:08,629 --> 00:10:13,091
If I was the same as ten years ago,
do you think I'd have worked with you?

147
00:10:15,677 --> 00:10:19,139
There's nothing to be scared of.
My calculations are never off.

148
00:10:19,223 --> 00:10:21,225
You, Ma Gong-bok, Seong-won, and me?

149
00:10:21,892 --> 00:10:25,229
We may be washed up,
but we'd never lose to Yoo In-gu.

150
00:10:25,354 --> 00:10:27,522
So don't you worry.

151
00:10:28,565 --> 00:10:30,275
Just stick to the plan.

152
00:10:31,693 --> 00:10:33,570
Then you won't get your ass kicked alone.

153
00:10:34,821 --> 00:10:35,864
Well, well.

154
00:10:36,615 --> 00:10:38,242
Now it feels like a real alliance.

155
00:10:39,326 --> 00:10:40,744
Fine, we've come this far.

156
00:10:41,912 --> 00:10:43,247
I'll trust you this once.

157
00:10:44,957 --> 00:10:45,958
Damn it.

158
00:11:05,644 --> 00:11:06,979
You guys go on ahead.

159
00:11:08,939 --> 00:11:10,232
What? You're not coming?

160
00:11:11,024 --> 00:11:12,818
You said we were doing a final check.

161
00:11:12,901 --> 00:11:15,112
No, there's somewhere I need to be.

162
00:11:15,237 --> 00:11:16,989
Where are you going all of a sudden?

163
00:11:18,949 --> 00:11:19,950
Something came up.

164
00:11:20,033 --> 00:11:23,245
The big bust is just around the corner,
and something came up?

165
00:11:23,328 --> 00:11:24,788
You think I have nothing to do?

166
00:11:24,871 --> 00:11:26,999
I've got a million things
to check before closing.

167
00:11:27,082 --> 00:11:29,960
We have a lot to go over.
Where are you going?

168
00:11:34,923 --> 00:11:35,924
It's all right.

169
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,676
Don't worry about it. Just go.

170
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,012
Go on. I'll take care of things here.

171
00:11:40,137 --> 00:11:41,596
Huh? What's gotten into you?

172
00:11:45,142 --> 00:11:48,437
- But what about the operation?
- I'll handle it. Let's go.

173
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,856
How can we do that without him?

174
00:11:50,939 --> 00:11:52,983
We've gone over it enough. We'll be fine.

175
00:11:53,066 --> 00:11:54,735
Yeah, but he's the one who planned it.

176
00:12:04,077 --> 00:12:06,830
You know where he went, don't you?

177
00:12:07,456 --> 00:12:10,250
He just went to take care of something.

178
00:12:10,334 --> 00:12:12,419
He just remembered he had an errand to run

179
00:12:12,502 --> 00:12:13,962
just hours before the operation?

180
00:12:14,504 --> 00:12:16,298
Be honest. Did something happen?

181
00:12:17,299 --> 00:12:18,967
It's not that.

182
00:12:19,051 --> 00:12:21,470
Gong-bok brought up family earlier.

183
00:12:21,595 --> 00:12:23,680
- I think it got to him.
- Family?

184
00:12:23,764 --> 00:12:25,307
What did I say about family?

185
00:12:25,932 --> 00:12:28,435
Oh, you mean
when I joked about his marriage?

186
00:12:29,478 --> 00:12:31,855
- So his marriage really is a sham?
- Don't ever say that!

187
00:12:32,814 --> 00:12:34,316
That's not it.

188
00:12:34,399 --> 00:12:36,777
It's Ho-myeong's first operation
since he's had a family.

189
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:38,862
So he probably has a lot on his mind.

190
00:12:38,945 --> 00:12:41,782
He knows better than anyone
just how evil Han Gyeong-wook is.

191
00:12:43,158 --> 00:12:46,244
You mean he knows him?
Jeong Ho-myeong and Han Gyeong-wook?

192
00:12:47,079 --> 00:12:48,997
Did they know each other
before the ferry case?

193
00:12:54,628 --> 00:12:57,672
- I shouldn't have said anything.
- No, you have to tell us.

194
00:12:57,756 --> 00:13:00,926
The guy's pulling a stunt like this
right before the operation.

195
00:13:01,051 --> 00:13:02,969
We have a right to know why, don't we?

196
00:13:05,722 --> 00:13:07,724
When Ho-myeong was with the NIS

197
00:13:08,475 --> 00:13:11,186
he used to work on the same team
as Han Gyeong-wook.

198
00:13:11,269 --> 00:13:14,272
- They were on the same team?
- Yeah.

199
00:13:16,525 --> 00:13:19,486
For a long time, until that incident.

200
00:13:19,569 --> 00:13:20,987
They were partners.

201
00:13:21,696 --> 00:13:24,866
12 YEARS AGO

202
00:13:43,885 --> 00:13:44,928
I'm in.

203
00:13:46,179 --> 00:13:47,597
You sure the mole is here?

204
00:13:47,681 --> 00:13:50,308
Positive.
That mole has leaked crucial intel.

205
00:13:50,392 --> 00:13:52,352
It's gotten a lot of our agents killed.

206
00:13:52,436 --> 00:13:55,897
We can't let a traitor like that run away
without paying for what he's done.

207
00:13:55,981 --> 00:13:58,191
You're to shoot to kill on sight.

208
00:13:58,275 --> 00:13:59,651
Roger that.

209
00:14:36,563 --> 00:14:38,231
You know why I'm here, don't you?

210
00:14:56,208 --> 00:14:57,876
- You...
- Ho-myeong.

211
00:14:58,752 --> 00:15:01,421
- Just listen to me.
- It was you?

212
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:05,592
- The traitor who sold out his own people?
- No. You know me.

213
00:15:06,134 --> 00:15:10,639
You know how hard I worked
for the sake of our nation.

214
00:15:10,972 --> 00:15:13,183
Then why are you not in North Korea?

215
00:15:14,017 --> 00:15:16,770
Deputy Director Han confirmed it himself.

216
00:15:17,604 --> 00:15:21,066
That the traitor would be here today
to sell the intel on our agents.

217
00:15:21,816 --> 00:15:23,151
Ho-myeong.

218
00:15:24,486 --> 00:15:25,946
You're being played by him.

219
00:15:27,405 --> 00:15:28,490
He framed me.

220
00:15:29,282 --> 00:15:30,825
He forced me to live on the run.

221
00:15:32,077 --> 00:15:34,079
- It was Deputy Director Han.
- Shut up.

222
00:15:35,038 --> 00:15:36,039
Why would he do that?

223
00:15:36,122 --> 00:15:39,042
Han is up to something.

224
00:15:40,544 --> 00:15:42,170
He thought I'd figure it out.

225
00:15:44,923 --> 00:15:46,174
So he's trying to get rid of me.

226
00:15:47,509 --> 00:15:49,261
What exactly is he up to?

227
00:15:49,803 --> 00:15:52,097
- Can you prove it?
- Well...

228
00:15:58,019 --> 00:15:59,020
Ho-myeong.

229
00:15:59,896 --> 00:16:00,897
Ten minutes.

230
00:16:01,898 --> 00:16:03,775
- What?
- Just give me ten minutes.

231
00:16:06,236 --> 00:16:07,237
My daughter will be here.

232
00:16:08,113 --> 00:16:10,407
I only saw her as a baby six years ago.

233
00:16:11,491 --> 00:16:12,534
Please.

234
00:16:13,535 --> 00:16:15,120
Let me have one dinner with her.

235
00:16:18,707 --> 00:16:21,084
- You're lying.
- I'm not lying.

236
00:16:22,002 --> 00:16:23,169
Just ten minutes.

237
00:16:24,337 --> 00:16:26,256
She'll be here in ten minutes.

238
00:16:26,339 --> 00:16:29,759
We'll just have dinner together,
and I'll go with you.

239
00:16:31,344 --> 00:16:33,513
After that, you can do
whatever you want with me.

240
00:16:34,389 --> 00:16:35,390
Ho-myeong.

241
00:16:36,141 --> 00:16:37,434
I'll come with you

242
00:16:37,517 --> 00:16:38,560
and tell you all about Han's--

243
00:16:46,026 --> 00:16:47,277
Sir.

244
00:17:09,215 --> 00:17:12,093
I believe my orders
were to eliminate him on sight.

245
00:17:13,803 --> 00:17:16,806
I came by just in case. Good thing I did.

246
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:21,311
Jeong Ho-myeong, you're an agent.

247
00:17:21,936 --> 00:17:23,605
Did you seriously believe his crap?

248
00:17:23,688 --> 00:17:25,899
He used to be part of your team, sir.

249
00:17:26,650 --> 00:17:29,986
Shouldn't we have at least heard him out?

250
00:17:31,154 --> 00:17:32,656
Heard him out?

251
00:17:34,449 --> 00:17:35,617
It's just...

252
00:17:36,284 --> 00:17:39,621
He said he wasn't here to make a deal.
He said his daughter was coming.

253
00:17:40,872 --> 00:17:42,540
He said he'd come with us after they eat.

254
00:17:45,251 --> 00:17:46,878
And you believe that crap?

255
00:17:48,421 --> 00:17:49,923
Where is his daughter then?

256
00:17:54,302 --> 00:17:58,765
You know that such sentiments
are just a weakness for an agent.

257
00:18:03,311 --> 00:18:05,063
I've wasted enough time on this.

258
00:18:07,565 --> 00:18:08,900
Clean up this mess.

259
00:19:08,668 --> 00:19:10,754
That incident must've been
a huge shock to him.

260
00:19:10,837 --> 00:19:13,757
He asked to be taken off field duty
several times.

261
00:19:14,758 --> 00:19:16,092
But it was denied every time.

262
00:19:18,303 --> 00:19:21,556
If Han Gyeong-wook found out
that Ho-myeong is married and has a son...

263
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:23,725
There's no telling what he'd do.

264
00:19:24,517 --> 00:19:27,854
Ho-myeong never showed it,
but he must have been worried.

265
00:19:39,741 --> 00:19:42,160
You want me to pull out
from the restaurant?

266
00:19:42,243 --> 00:19:43,244
7 YEARS AGO

267
00:19:43,328 --> 00:19:44,871
Yeah.

268
00:19:44,954 --> 00:19:47,916
You've been here all this time
without a single sign of Bulgae.

269
00:19:48,041 --> 00:19:49,834
I know, but still.

270
00:19:51,461 --> 00:19:53,213
Is it really necessary to move?

271
00:19:53,296 --> 00:19:56,132
Staying in one place too long
could compromise your cover.

272
00:19:56,216 --> 00:19:57,550
You know that.

273
00:19:59,177 --> 00:20:01,971
It's time to move.
Start wrapping things up.

274
00:20:04,849 --> 00:20:06,351
Yeah. Okay.

275
00:20:08,937 --> 00:20:10,230
Wrap things up.

276
00:20:13,775 --> 00:20:14,776
There.

277
00:20:15,193 --> 00:20:17,654
- Here's your jjamppong.
- Thank you.

278
00:20:47,433 --> 00:20:49,602
- Hey, Ho-myeong.
- Yeah?

279
00:20:50,186 --> 00:20:53,982
I have to talk to you about something
after we close.

280
00:20:54,649 --> 00:20:56,401
- To me?
- Yeah.

281
00:21:02,657 --> 00:21:04,826
No, I'm not drinking.

282
00:21:05,785 --> 00:21:08,746
- Why not?
- Well, the thing is...

283
00:21:14,878 --> 00:21:15,920
Ho-myeong.

284
00:21:16,838 --> 00:21:19,173
Remember how I said
I haven't been feeling well lately?

285
00:21:19,799 --> 00:21:21,259
You're still not feeling well?

286
00:21:23,344 --> 00:21:24,762
Well...

287
00:21:24,846 --> 00:21:26,347
I'm pregnant.

288
00:21:37,150 --> 00:21:38,568
Pregnant?

289
00:21:40,194 --> 00:21:43,948
I went to the doctor yesterday.
I'm eight weeks in.

290
00:21:48,369 --> 00:21:50,788
I'm not telling you this to pressure you.

291
00:21:51,164 --> 00:21:53,041
I'll handle it.

292
00:21:53,166 --> 00:21:54,667
What do you mean you'll handle it?

293
00:21:57,170 --> 00:21:59,631
Honestly, you and I?

294
00:22:00,506 --> 00:22:04,677
What we have is just a fling, isn't it?

295
00:22:07,055 --> 00:22:08,431
What are you saying?

296
00:22:10,808 --> 00:22:15,730
We've been seeing each other
for a long time.

297
00:22:16,773 --> 00:22:18,274
But I don't know much about you.

298
00:22:19,525 --> 00:22:20,985
Barely anything, really.

299
00:22:21,986 --> 00:22:26,574
Like who you were before,
or why you came to Yeongseon Island.

300
00:22:27,492 --> 00:22:31,663
I've never even heard you mention
your parents, siblings, or friends.

301
00:22:33,164 --> 00:22:34,290
And you don't...

302
00:22:35,041 --> 00:22:37,085
You don't exactly have plans

303
00:22:37,835 --> 00:22:39,337
to tell me

304
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:42,590
about any of that, do you?

305
00:22:52,183 --> 00:22:55,937
I'm almost 40,
so having a baby is a bit...

306
00:22:56,854 --> 00:22:57,855
scary.

307
00:22:58,815 --> 00:23:01,651
And even if I had a baby,

308
00:23:01,734 --> 00:23:03,486
I'd have no idea how to raise it.

309
00:23:03,569 --> 00:23:05,238
Plus, I'm busy with the store.

310
00:23:06,239 --> 00:23:09,075
I've said what I needed to say,
so just enjoy your drink.

311
00:23:10,076 --> 00:23:11,327
I'm not drinking.

312
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:13,121
Huh?

313
00:23:16,916 --> 00:23:18,292
I won't drink alone.

314
00:23:19,836 --> 00:23:21,170
Let's drink after the baby is born.

315
00:23:25,133 --> 00:23:26,134
What...

316
00:23:26,968 --> 00:23:29,262
What do you mean by that?

317
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:32,306
Let's have this baby.

318
00:23:33,516 --> 00:23:36,978
Is it really that simple for you?

319
00:23:37,061 --> 00:23:38,396
It's not.

320
00:23:40,565 --> 00:23:41,858
The truth is...

321
00:23:43,609 --> 00:23:45,361
My parents passed away when I was young.

322
00:23:47,113 --> 00:23:48,740
So I never had a family.

323
00:23:50,366 --> 00:23:53,036
I never thought about things
like marriage or kids.

324
00:23:54,537 --> 00:23:56,831
I've never even thought
about starting my own family.

325
00:23:58,416 --> 00:24:00,835
But when you just told me
you were pregnant...

326
00:24:01,586 --> 00:24:02,587
I mean...

327
00:24:03,379 --> 00:24:05,465
I don't know what this feeling is.

328
00:24:07,050 --> 00:24:08,134
But it made me think...

329
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:13,306
That no matter what happens

330
00:24:14,766 --> 00:24:16,350
I want to be with you and our child.

331
00:24:19,437 --> 00:24:21,814
Let's get married, O-ran.

332
00:24:46,130 --> 00:24:48,091
Ho-myeong, why are you out here?

333
00:24:48,174 --> 00:24:51,052
- Why aren't you coming in?
- Oh, you scared me.

334
00:24:51,135 --> 00:24:53,262
Didn't you come here
to make up with O-ran?

335
00:24:59,143 --> 00:25:00,978
You brought the letter, right?

336
00:25:02,063 --> 00:25:04,148
- No.
- What? Why not?

337
00:25:04,232 --> 00:25:05,358
Well, I just...

338
00:25:06,359 --> 00:25:10,822
- I didn't know what to write.
- You still don't get O-ran?

339
00:25:10,905 --> 00:25:15,118
She'll forgive you
if you just say the right things.

340
00:25:15,201 --> 00:25:17,370
She's that easygoing, just like me.

341
00:25:18,996 --> 00:25:22,583
Well, this time,
I don't know if a few words will do.

342
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,670
And I'm the one at fault.

343
00:25:25,795 --> 00:25:28,548
I think I'll just make her angrier.

344
00:25:33,427 --> 00:25:36,973
Do you know
why I came to Yeongseon Island?

345
00:25:38,641 --> 00:25:39,851
You said it was your hometown.

346
00:25:39,934 --> 00:25:41,352
It's not.

347
00:25:41,435 --> 00:25:43,563
I was going to open a store in Seoul.

348
00:25:43,646 --> 00:25:46,274
But I lost the money in a scam,
so I had no choice.

349
00:25:46,816 --> 00:25:47,817
What?

350
00:25:48,818 --> 00:25:52,613
I couldn't tell my wife.
My pride wouldn't let me.

351
00:25:53,281 --> 00:25:55,283
So I just lied to her.

352
00:25:55,366 --> 00:25:58,536
I told her wanted to settle down
in my hometown.

353
00:26:00,413 --> 00:26:04,000
My wife must have suspected something.

354
00:26:04,083 --> 00:26:05,710
But she didn't say a word.

355
00:26:05,793 --> 00:26:08,588
Even though she was pregnant,
she followed me without a complaint.

356
00:26:09,672 --> 00:26:12,425
I figured if she knew I'd been scammed,
she'd only be heartbroken.

357
00:26:12,508 --> 00:26:13,968
So I kept it from her.

358
00:26:14,051 --> 00:26:18,431
I thought I'd tell her
once the restaurant had found its place.

359
00:26:18,514 --> 00:26:19,807
But then...

360
00:26:20,933 --> 00:26:22,560
I never got to tell her.

361
00:26:26,898 --> 00:26:29,442
I should have just told her.

362
00:26:30,568 --> 00:26:32,778
Why did she work so hard every day?

363
00:26:32,862 --> 00:26:34,155
She wasn't well.

364
00:26:35,281 --> 00:26:37,742
She never even made time
to go to a hospital.

365
00:26:42,205 --> 00:26:43,331
I wish I'd told her.

366
00:26:44,332 --> 00:26:47,001
Maybe she would've hated me
a little less when she passed.

367
00:26:52,256 --> 00:26:54,383
Don't leave any stupid regrets like I did.

368
00:26:54,467 --> 00:26:56,219
Be open with each other.

369
00:26:56,302 --> 00:26:59,347
That's what marriage is all about, right?

370
00:27:00,097 --> 00:27:01,349
Don't let O-ran...

371
00:27:02,266 --> 00:27:04,101
Don't let my daughter
be upset for so long.

372
00:27:07,396 --> 00:27:11,234
- Yes, I understand.
- Yeah? Let's go right now.

373
00:27:11,317 --> 00:27:13,945
Right now, I have something
I need to sort out.

374
00:27:14,779 --> 00:27:18,074
Next time I'm around, I'll tell her.

375
00:27:18,157 --> 00:27:23,996
I'll tell O-ran everything
that I haven't been able to.

376
00:27:25,790 --> 00:27:27,041
Geez.

377
00:27:28,751 --> 00:27:29,835
You know, right?

378
00:27:30,544 --> 00:27:32,046
An apology is all about timing.

379
00:27:33,506 --> 00:27:36,092
Yes. I won't be too late.

380
00:27:47,979 --> 00:27:51,941
It's been forever
since I've had the spotlight.

381
00:27:52,024 --> 00:27:53,234
I'm getting nervous.

382
00:27:55,069 --> 00:27:57,029
Give me one last update, will you?

383
00:27:57,780 --> 00:27:59,740
You've cut off
all funding for the orphanage, right?

384
00:28:01,158 --> 00:28:03,119
Oh, you shouldn't have.

385
00:28:10,626 --> 00:28:14,255
Thanks to Deputy Director Han,
it all went smoothly.

386
00:28:14,839 --> 00:28:15,840
Sir!

387
00:28:15,923 --> 00:28:19,135
We could say they didn't qualify
due to their outdated facilities.

388
00:28:19,218 --> 00:28:22,054
It's not even
the scheduled inspection date.

389
00:28:22,138 --> 00:28:24,682
It's a surprise inspection, ma'am.

390
00:28:24,765 --> 00:28:27,059
If we gave you a notice,
how would it be a surprise?

391
00:28:28,519 --> 00:28:30,521
Their financial situation is obvious.

392
00:28:30,604 --> 00:28:32,565
It's true that
the facilities are outdated.

393
00:28:32,648 --> 00:28:36,861
But still, if you do this so suddenly,
where are our children supposed to go?

394
00:28:36,944 --> 00:28:40,072
In any case, we have issued a warning
as per protocol.

395
00:28:40,156 --> 00:28:42,408
You can either use your own money
to make the repairs

396
00:28:42,491 --> 00:28:43,784
or shut the place down.

397
00:28:43,868 --> 00:28:45,286
Whatever you need to do.

398
00:28:45,369 --> 00:28:49,999
With no money to fix up the place,
they'll end up doing as we intended.

399
00:28:50,082 --> 00:28:52,960
- What about donors?
- They didn't have any major ones.

400
00:28:53,044 --> 00:28:56,756
Besides government subsidies,
it's all small donations from individuals.

401
00:28:56,839 --> 00:29:00,426
And most of that is Kim Seon-jung
and his wife's personal funds.

402
00:29:01,135 --> 00:29:04,138
That's why it's a problem
when you're too squeaky clean.

403
00:29:04,972 --> 00:29:06,557
Okay, good job.

404
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:08,184
Now then.

405
00:29:08,934 --> 00:29:12,646
Shall I go and help myself
to the feast that's been laid out?

406
00:29:17,109 --> 00:29:18,861
Hello, sir.

407
00:29:18,944 --> 00:29:21,781
- How have you been?
- Good. How about you?

408
00:29:21,864 --> 00:29:22,907
That's good.

409
00:29:22,990 --> 00:29:24,450
Why can't we take out a loan?

410
00:29:24,533 --> 00:29:25,576
I'm sorry.

411
00:29:25,659 --> 00:29:27,828
But our decision is based on an evaluation

412
00:29:27,912 --> 00:29:29,872
of your credit rating
and collateral value.

413
00:29:29,955 --> 00:29:33,542
Your loan application
was denied in our internal review.

414
00:29:33,626 --> 00:29:36,170
But the manager said it was possible.

415
00:29:36,253 --> 00:29:38,839
Could you please check one more time?

416
00:29:43,177 --> 00:29:45,388
Excuse me, sir.

417
00:29:48,349 --> 00:29:51,352
- Oh, ma'am, what brings you here?
- Hello, sir.

418
00:29:51,435 --> 00:29:55,272
Ma'am, please, let's not do this here.
You can talk to me.

419
00:29:55,356 --> 00:29:56,524
Please.

420
00:29:56,607 --> 00:30:01,070
Why was the loan suddenly denied?
We're going to have to shut down.

421
00:30:01,153 --> 00:30:03,739
What are we supposed to do
with the children?

422
00:30:03,823 --> 00:30:05,324
Ah, excuse me.

423
00:30:06,158 --> 00:30:10,037
- What children?
- Oh, this lady runs an orphanage.

424
00:30:10,121 --> 00:30:12,206
And it seems there's been
a misunderstanding.

425
00:30:13,374 --> 00:30:17,336
Well, if you don't mind,
may I listen in on what she has to say?

426
00:30:17,795 --> 00:30:21,090
It's just that I don't quite understand
what's going on.

427
00:30:21,173 --> 00:30:25,928
This lady seems like a wonderful person
who dedicates herself to society.

428
00:30:26,512 --> 00:30:28,722
What's the reason
her loan was suddenly denied?

429
00:30:29,473 --> 00:30:31,392
Well, the thing is...

430
00:30:31,934 --> 00:30:35,729
When it comes to loans,
there are various policy-related factors.

431
00:30:36,605 --> 00:30:38,732
Exactly, those policies.

432
00:30:38,816 --> 00:30:42,319
They don't just change overnight, do they?
What do you think?

433
00:30:42,403 --> 00:30:45,531
Exactly.
You said it wasn't a problem last time.

434
00:30:45,614 --> 00:30:48,826
Sir, are you sure
you've reviewed this properly?

435
00:30:48,909 --> 00:30:50,035
Uh, well, that's...

436
00:30:50,119 --> 00:30:53,622
I've never seen a bank
change a loan policy overnight.

437
00:30:54,039 --> 00:30:56,000
I'm rapidly losing my faith
in this establishment.

438
00:30:56,709 --> 00:30:59,712
Who knows?
I could be in that lady's shoes.

439
00:31:00,379 --> 00:31:02,882
And you might
just flip on me just as easily.

440
00:31:02,965 --> 00:31:04,258
No, I would...

441
00:31:05,134 --> 00:31:06,719
That's... Ms. Kim.

442
00:31:07,303 --> 00:31:09,680
Bring me the documents
for the lady's loan.

443
00:31:09,763 --> 00:31:12,224
- I'll take a look myself.
- Yes, sir. Right away.

444
00:31:12,308 --> 00:31:13,350
Quickly.

445
00:31:15,978 --> 00:31:17,188
Excuse me.

446
00:31:18,856 --> 00:31:21,192
I never got a chance to thank you.

447
00:31:21,275 --> 00:31:22,776
Thank you so much.

448
00:31:22,860 --> 00:31:25,529
Oh, it was nothing.
Was everything resolved?

449
00:31:25,654 --> 00:31:27,031
Yes.

450
00:31:27,114 --> 00:31:29,158
Thanks to you,
I think the loan will be approved.

451
00:31:30,242 --> 00:31:33,913
- I can't thank you enough.
- Oh, never mind, never mind.

452
00:31:34,371 --> 00:31:38,083
You were so worried
the children would wind up on the streets.

453
00:31:39,502 --> 00:31:41,128
It reminded me of my past.

454
00:31:42,755 --> 00:31:45,382
When I was young,
my father's business failed.

455
00:31:45,508 --> 00:31:47,343
And I was homeless in the Philippines.

456
00:31:47,426 --> 00:31:49,178
Oh, no. Really?

457
00:31:49,261 --> 00:31:52,473
I made a promise to myself back then.

458
00:31:53,516 --> 00:31:57,186
That I would never turn my back
on someone in need.

459
00:31:57,478 --> 00:32:00,481
But I'd forgotten all about it
just because I got a little busy.

460
00:32:00,564 --> 00:32:04,693
You clearly haven't.
You helped our children so much today.

461
00:32:04,818 --> 00:32:06,737
Not at all. On the contrary.

462
00:32:07,571 --> 00:32:11,617
Meeting you today has made me
reflect on a lot of things.

463
00:32:11,700 --> 00:32:14,161
I've been so focused on getting ahead

464
00:32:14,245 --> 00:32:17,706
that I haven't looked
at the world around me.

465
00:32:17,790 --> 00:32:19,583
And frankly, I'm ashamed of myself.

466
00:32:21,877 --> 00:32:23,337
Which brings me to my point.

467
00:32:23,420 --> 00:32:25,422
You don't have to say yes.

468
00:32:25,506 --> 00:32:29,468
But would it be okay
if I sent a small gift to the children?

469
00:32:29,552 --> 00:32:32,221
- What?
- Ah, a gift. Yes?

470
00:32:33,347 --> 00:32:35,766
As long as you follow
the proper procedure.

471
00:32:35,849 --> 00:32:39,687
Oh, it's not that big of a gift
that'd require formal procedures.

472
00:32:40,271 --> 00:32:42,982
As long as you say yes, that is.

473
00:32:44,984 --> 00:32:48,028
We try to run our organization
as transparently as possible.

474
00:32:48,153 --> 00:32:52,241
We don't accept any private donations
of cash or goods.

475
00:32:52,324 --> 00:32:55,035
I'm sorry, but we'll only have to
accept your kind words.

476
00:32:55,119 --> 00:32:56,370
No.

477
00:32:56,453 --> 00:33:00,541
It's really not a big deal at all,
so I'm actually a bit embarrassed.

478
00:33:01,834 --> 00:33:05,462
Have we disposed of all the old books
from our hotel lounge?

479
00:33:05,546 --> 00:33:07,673
- Not yet.
- All right.

480
00:33:08,382 --> 00:33:11,635
It may not be much,
but what if I gave them these books?

481
00:33:11,719 --> 00:33:14,138
The idea just popped into my head.

482
00:33:14,263 --> 00:33:17,683
- Oh, the books?
- Yes. The books.

483
00:33:17,766 --> 00:33:21,103
It's not money or material things.
Just food for thought?

484
00:33:22,229 --> 00:33:26,567
It's just a few old books.
Would that be a problem too?

485
00:33:30,154 --> 00:33:32,281
WE OPPOSE YEONGSEON REDEVELOPMENT

486
00:33:57,848 --> 00:34:01,060
It was brief,
but the way he moved was not ordinary.

487
00:34:04,855 --> 00:34:06,523
And he has amnesia?

488
00:34:07,399 --> 00:34:09,985
There's so much
that's suspicious about him.

489
00:34:15,824 --> 00:34:20,329
Look. Prosecutor Gang has been
staring at Je-sun like that for a while.

490
00:34:20,412 --> 00:34:23,916
Something's definitely
going on between them.

491
00:34:24,833 --> 00:34:27,753
No way.
She just looks like she wants a fight.

492
00:34:27,836 --> 00:34:29,046
What would you know?

493
00:34:29,546 --> 00:34:30,589
You've never had a man.

494
00:34:39,098 --> 00:34:41,934
Mr. Bong.
Something happened between you two, right?

495
00:34:44,478 --> 00:34:46,146
Nothing happened.

496
00:34:46,230 --> 00:34:48,816
I was quite the heartbreaker
back in my day.

497
00:34:49,483 --> 00:34:51,819
When a woman gives you a look like that?

498
00:34:51,944 --> 00:34:55,280
It's either you owe her money,
or she's into you.

499
00:34:58,909 --> 00:35:00,619
It's so delicious.

500
00:35:03,706 --> 00:35:04,873
Be honest.

501
00:35:04,957 --> 00:35:06,792
You're into her too, aren't you?

502
00:35:06,875 --> 00:35:10,087
Come on, it's not like that. It's just...

503
00:35:11,171 --> 00:35:13,507
I mean, we've gotten kind of close.

504
00:35:14,049 --> 00:35:18,053
I'm just gonna bring the Sergeant
some soup in.

505
00:35:25,269 --> 00:35:26,854
Busy, busy.

506
00:35:28,439 --> 00:35:29,773
This was so delicious.

507
00:35:30,774 --> 00:35:32,151
I'll do the dishes tomorrow.

508
00:35:44,747 --> 00:35:46,248
Eat up.

509
00:35:49,752 --> 00:35:52,421
Hey, mister. Could you untie me, please?

510
00:35:52,504 --> 00:35:54,673
I'm not a criminal. What is this?

511
00:35:54,757 --> 00:35:56,133
Eat up.

512
00:35:58,719 --> 00:36:00,846
Come on, how can I eat
with my hands tied like this?

513
00:36:07,728 --> 00:36:09,104
Eat up.

514
00:36:11,940 --> 00:36:13,692
Damn it.

515
00:36:13,776 --> 00:36:15,694
This is a felony, you know that?

516
00:36:15,778 --> 00:36:20,449
The real felony is what you
and the Heaven Capital guys committed.

517
00:36:21,033 --> 00:36:24,119
Fine, don't eat if you don't want to.
What a waste of rice. Jeez.

518
00:36:24,828 --> 00:36:26,163
Wait, wait.

519
00:36:26,914 --> 00:36:30,375
Wait, are you the martial arts master
Heaven Capital was looking for?

520
00:36:30,501 --> 00:36:32,211
You fought them 17 to 1? Or was it 18?

521
00:36:32,294 --> 00:36:34,213
And the way you moved yesterday...

522
00:36:34,296 --> 00:36:35,589
It is you!

523
00:36:35,672 --> 00:36:36,799
Listen, sir.

524
00:36:36,882 --> 00:36:38,175
It's a pleasure to meet you.

525
00:36:38,258 --> 00:36:39,426
Please untie me.

526
00:36:39,510 --> 00:36:41,929
If you let me go,
I'll have a word with those guys.

527
00:36:42,012 --> 00:36:44,807
I'll tell them to stop chasing you.

528
00:36:44,890 --> 00:36:45,933
I promise. Okay?

529
00:36:50,270 --> 00:36:51,897
Just, uh... Eat your food.

530
00:37:11,458 --> 00:37:12,960
What the...

531
00:37:14,044 --> 00:37:15,254
What are you doing?

532
00:37:17,714 --> 00:37:20,467
Oh, I felt so dizzy
that I had to lean against the door.

533
00:37:25,472 --> 00:37:26,473
Goodness.

534
00:37:38,777 --> 00:37:39,778
Go ahead and eat.

535
00:37:45,617 --> 00:37:50,289
Here we go.

536
00:37:55,711 --> 00:37:56,962
You look cheerful.

537
00:37:57,421 --> 00:37:59,715
Feeling better
now that the loan came through?

538
00:38:00,716 --> 00:38:03,385
Of course. I was worried sick.

539
00:38:03,719 --> 00:38:08,307
Guess what? Someone I met at the bank
wants to make a donation.

540
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,351
A donation? Who?

541
00:38:11,435 --> 00:38:15,480
Chairman Do Hyeon-tae of the Heaven Hotel.
He said they have used books.

542
00:38:15,606 --> 00:38:18,025
He'd rather donate them to the kids
than throw them away.

543
00:38:20,277 --> 00:38:21,320
Do Hyeon-tae...

544
00:38:22,654 --> 00:38:23,989
The Chairman of Heaven Casino?

545
00:38:25,866 --> 00:38:28,869
He's never shown any interest
in public service.

546
00:38:29,286 --> 00:38:31,079
Why suddenly make a donation?

547
00:38:33,749 --> 00:38:34,917
That's odd.

548
00:38:37,836 --> 00:38:40,255
Honey, you have to turn it down.

549
00:38:41,757 --> 00:38:42,758
What?

550
00:38:43,508 --> 00:38:46,303
It's a book donation, not money.

551
00:38:46,386 --> 00:38:50,515
Still, who knows
what the man is really after?

552
00:38:50,599 --> 00:38:53,310
Anyway, don't take anything from him,
books or otherwise.

553
00:38:53,393 --> 00:38:55,604
You've really turned into a politician,
haven't you?

554
00:38:55,687 --> 00:38:57,731
It was a kind offer.

555
00:38:57,814 --> 00:38:59,858
And you can't see it
as anything but suspicious?

556
00:38:59,942 --> 00:39:02,277
That's not it.
I'm just saying we should be careful.

557
00:39:02,361 --> 00:39:05,489
It's just a few used books.
What is there to be so careful about?

558
00:39:05,572 --> 00:39:08,450
Should the children go without books
because of your political ambitions?

559
00:39:17,417 --> 00:39:20,170
You're right. I overreacted.

560
00:39:20,253 --> 00:39:23,340
It's just a few used books.
Take them. All right?

561
00:39:23,924 --> 00:39:25,926
- Really?
- Yeah.

562
00:39:34,434 --> 00:39:38,730
Chairman, we've received the used books.

563
00:39:38,814 --> 00:39:41,108
Thank you for your generous donation.

564
00:39:42,234 --> 00:39:43,860
Your kindness

565
00:39:43,944 --> 00:39:47,322
will be food for the soul
for everyone here.

566
00:39:52,285 --> 00:39:54,246
The package is delivered.

567
00:39:56,790 --> 00:39:59,835
I made a special selection
from my most prized collections.

568
00:40:01,086 --> 00:40:03,296
You didn't just drop them off
and leave, did you?

569
00:40:04,423 --> 00:40:05,924
Of course not.

570
00:40:06,008 --> 00:40:08,969
I've already spoken to an employee.

571
00:40:10,512 --> 00:40:12,889
I told him he'd be ruined
by gambling debts

572
00:40:12,973 --> 00:40:15,642
if he didn't get rid of
those paintings for us.

573
00:40:16,476 --> 00:40:19,438
It's to be sold off without her knowing,
and the money will be discreetly deposited

574
00:40:19,521 --> 00:40:22,482
into the organization's bank account
as a donation.

575
00:40:22,566 --> 00:40:24,943
Just push the button

576
00:40:25,027 --> 00:40:27,863
and Kim Seon-jung will no longer be

577
00:40:27,946 --> 00:40:29,990
the honest mayoral candidate
everyone loves.

578
00:40:30,073 --> 00:40:33,493
He'll be a man who used a charity
to raise illegal political funds.

579
00:40:33,952 --> 00:40:36,413
A corrupt politician
who's no better than trash.

580
00:40:39,875 --> 00:40:41,918
- Well done.
- Thank you.

581
00:40:42,502 --> 00:40:43,545
So...

582
00:40:44,046 --> 00:40:45,172
Shall I set off the package?

583
00:40:45,297 --> 00:40:46,673
If we're going to set it off

584
00:40:47,632 --> 00:40:49,551
it might as well be a good show.

585
00:40:50,093 --> 00:40:51,970
- What do you mean?
- Baek.

586
00:40:52,345 --> 00:40:53,346
Yes.

587
00:40:53,847 --> 00:40:57,017
Let's go grab some soup soon.

588
00:40:57,142 --> 00:40:58,310
Understood.

589
00:41:04,649 --> 00:41:06,151
Hey, what are you talking about?

590
00:41:06,234 --> 00:41:07,611
I was planning on going.

591
00:41:08,111 --> 00:41:10,781
But we've been after this broker
for the last three months.

592
00:41:11,073 --> 00:41:13,283
Hey, this is a huge case.

593
00:41:14,785 --> 00:41:16,203
Okay, just listen.

594
00:41:16,953 --> 00:41:19,164
If you can't make it,
at least send someone else.

595
00:41:19,247 --> 00:41:21,249
This broker is a big deal too.

596
00:41:21,541 --> 00:41:23,251
Plus, it's the chief's orders.

597
00:41:23,335 --> 00:41:24,878
Everyone here is on it.

598
00:41:24,961 --> 00:41:26,171
I'll be right behind you.

599
00:41:26,254 --> 00:41:27,255
Anyway...

600
00:41:27,339 --> 00:41:29,132
Please just gather some evidence for now.

601
00:41:29,216 --> 00:41:30,759
I'll be there as soon as I'm done.

602
00:41:30,842 --> 00:41:33,804
Screw the evidence.
You should be raiding the place!

603
00:41:33,887 --> 00:41:34,888
Hello?

604
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:43,396
I thought they were just stealing money,
but they're bringing in drugs too.

605
00:41:44,439 --> 00:41:47,484
- You're the worst kind of scum.
- Look.

606
00:41:47,567 --> 00:41:50,487
These corrupt cops
and the Heaven Capital guys...

607
00:41:50,570 --> 00:41:55,075
If Prosecutor Gang links them to drugs,
can we really round them all up?

608
00:41:55,659 --> 00:41:57,577
We should be able to, right?

609
00:41:57,661 --> 00:41:59,704
It'll clean up the precinct, for sure.

610
00:41:59,788 --> 00:42:04,417
If they all go to prison,
everything they did will be revealed.

611
00:42:04,501 --> 00:42:06,753
If things go well,
I might get my house back.

612
00:42:07,838 --> 00:42:08,839
Hey, I'm sorry.

613
00:42:09,756 --> 00:42:12,592
I don't think the raid we planned
with the detectives today

614
00:42:12,676 --> 00:42:13,677
is going to happen.

615
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:15,887
- Why not?
- What?

616
00:42:15,971 --> 00:42:18,390
So, are we supposed to
just sit here and watch?

617
00:42:18,473 --> 00:42:20,350
Oh, no. I'll go alone if I have to.

618
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:23,186
I have to secure evidence
for there to be a next step.

619
00:42:23,478 --> 00:42:25,772
- All by yourself?
- Want to come with me then?

620
00:42:26,565 --> 00:42:29,025
Mi-kyung, would you mind coming with me?

621
00:42:29,109 --> 00:42:30,360
- Okay.
- Wait!

622
00:42:30,986 --> 00:42:32,863
I have to go too. I'm no civilian.

623
00:42:33,113 --> 00:42:35,407
- I'll be useful.
- I'm coming, too.

624
00:42:35,490 --> 00:42:37,826
I have to catch them to get my house back.

625
00:42:37,909 --> 00:42:39,828
I'll do anything. Please let me.

626
00:42:39,911 --> 00:42:43,915
Hold on.
That place is extremely dangerous.

627
00:42:44,457 --> 00:42:46,626
Then that's all the more reason
for us to go.

628
00:42:46,710 --> 00:42:48,837
We can't send you off all alone.

629
00:42:50,714 --> 00:42:51,715
- Right?
- Yes.

630
00:42:57,304 --> 00:42:58,847
- Welcome back, Boss!
- Welcome back, Boss!

631
00:42:59,472 --> 00:43:00,599
Is this everyone?

632
00:43:00,682 --> 00:43:01,683
Yes, Boss.

633
00:43:03,727 --> 00:43:07,564
As I told you before,
we must move without Han and Do noticing.

634
00:43:08,356 --> 00:43:09,357
This is the best we can do.

635
00:43:09,774 --> 00:43:12,611
Han and Do.
Those two are always getting in the way.

636
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:14,529
Don't worry, sir.

637
00:43:14,613 --> 00:43:17,449
I have about thirty kids
on standby at the port.

638
00:43:17,866 --> 00:43:21,620
Martial arts master or not,
he can't handle that many people alone.

639
00:43:22,287 --> 00:43:24,122
Gotta make do with what we've got.

640
00:43:24,873 --> 00:43:27,375
Today is a historic day for the Ingu Sect.

641
00:43:28,210 --> 00:43:30,253
Anyone who screws up will die at my hand.

642
00:43:31,421 --> 00:43:34,216
- So you'd better stay sharp!
- Yes, Boss!

643
00:43:41,223 --> 00:43:43,225
- Hey, you're here.
- Hey, Jin-su.

644
00:43:43,350 --> 00:43:45,644
- Nam-il's here too.
- Heard the pay was good.

645
00:43:49,856 --> 00:43:53,568
- Why did you bring Nam-il?
- He said he was desperate for cash.

646
00:43:54,236 --> 00:43:55,237
Just cut him some slack.

647
00:43:56,196 --> 00:43:58,782
Hey, but what are we even doing here?

648
00:44:00,325 --> 00:44:02,285
- Why do we need these tools?
- Beats me.

649
00:44:37,946 --> 00:44:39,072
Evening, Boss!

650
00:44:39,781 --> 00:44:41,283
This kid's got some fight in him.

651
00:44:41,366 --> 00:44:43,410
- Get your head up.
- Yes, Boss!

652
00:44:43,868 --> 00:44:46,037
- Is everyone here?
- Yes! They're all here.

653
00:44:46,121 --> 00:44:47,747
- Okay. To your posts.
- To your posts!

654
00:44:52,294 --> 00:44:53,545
Listen up.

655
00:44:53,628 --> 00:44:57,340
A very important package
is arriving today for the Ingu Sect.

656
00:44:57,465 --> 00:45:01,886
Your job is to secure said package.

657
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:03,805
And to make sure no one steals it.

658
00:45:05,098 --> 00:45:06,558
Those of you who do well today

659
00:45:07,392 --> 00:45:10,937
will be made full-time members
of the Ingu Sect with full benefits.

660
00:45:11,021 --> 00:45:12,981
- Got it?
- Yes, sir!

661
00:45:15,859 --> 00:45:17,277
What's this kid's problem?

662
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:18,528
Hey, move over.

663
00:45:20,572 --> 00:45:21,573
What?

664
00:45:22,782 --> 00:45:23,825
Huh?

665
00:45:24,784 --> 00:45:25,827
Hey, you punk. Get over here.

666
00:45:26,703 --> 00:45:29,247
- Why?
- Get over here. Hey, grab him.

667
00:45:29,331 --> 00:45:30,790
Hey, get him!

668
00:45:34,753 --> 00:45:36,129
Get over here.

669
00:45:37,922 --> 00:45:38,923
Boss.

670
00:45:41,593 --> 00:45:43,345
Aren't you
the martial arts master's nephew?

671
00:45:43,428 --> 00:45:44,679
Huh?

672
00:45:44,763 --> 00:45:46,264
- No, I'm not.
- It is, Boss.

673
00:45:46,514 --> 00:45:48,933
- You've got the wrong guy.
- I know it's you.

674
00:45:49,642 --> 00:45:51,644
What did I tell you? I was right.

675
00:45:51,728 --> 00:45:53,730
The martial arts master is here.

676
00:45:54,731 --> 00:45:58,401
He even planted his nephew as a mole.
He really came prepared.

677
00:45:58,985 --> 00:46:01,112
- What should we do, Boss?
- What else?

678
00:46:02,155 --> 00:46:03,948
The winning hand just fell into our hands.

679
00:46:04,032 --> 00:46:05,450
We just gratefully accept it.

680
00:46:07,660 --> 00:46:10,372
You're a little adorable rat, aren't you?

681
00:46:30,850 --> 00:46:34,270
Man, it feels great to be
out in the field again.

682
00:46:35,522 --> 00:46:36,731
So what do we do now?

683
00:46:37,482 --> 00:46:40,110
Do we mess up
those Heaven Capital guys now?

684
00:46:41,194 --> 00:46:42,487
Sorry, guys.

685
00:46:42,570 --> 00:46:44,656
I think I'd better go alone from here.

686
00:46:44,739 --> 00:46:46,699
But what are you going to do on your own?

687
00:46:46,783 --> 00:46:49,411
What? Why?
I was hoping to finally get some action.

688
00:46:49,494 --> 00:46:53,623
If we move as a group out here,
we'll be way too noticeable.

689
00:46:53,706 --> 00:46:55,875
I'll go in alone and secure the evidence.

690
00:46:55,959 --> 00:46:59,129
- You can wait in the car.
- Wait, just a moment.

691
00:47:00,964 --> 00:47:01,965
Come on.

692
00:47:04,801 --> 00:47:05,844
Listen.

693
00:47:06,928 --> 00:47:08,096
In case anything happens

694
00:47:09,222 --> 00:47:10,390
use this radio.

695
00:47:10,473 --> 00:47:11,474
I'll come running.

696
00:47:11,558 --> 00:47:13,435
Thank you. I'll be right back.

697
00:47:19,190 --> 00:47:21,568
- We would be noticeable.
- Very.

698
00:47:29,117 --> 00:47:31,411
But I really think I should follow her.

699
00:47:31,494 --> 00:47:34,539
- She said not to.
- She's in no condition for this.

700
00:47:35,290 --> 00:47:38,334
She's still not fully recovered.
Someone should be with her. I'll go.

701
00:47:40,420 --> 00:47:41,713
Okay.

702
00:47:41,921 --> 00:47:44,007
- I'll be right back. Just wait here.
- Wait.

703
00:47:44,090 --> 00:47:45,175
Prosecutor Gang!

704
00:47:45,717 --> 00:47:46,843
See that?

705
00:47:47,093 --> 00:47:48,761
There's something going on between them.

706
00:47:59,856 --> 00:48:00,857
Are you okay?

707
00:48:01,691 --> 00:48:02,692
Yeah.

708
00:48:11,826 --> 00:48:14,621
- Is it all in there?
- Have I ever let you down?

709
00:48:15,538 --> 00:48:16,539
You can see for yourself.

710
00:48:36,351 --> 00:48:39,062
By the way,
why'd you call in so many people?

711
00:48:39,771 --> 00:48:42,941
- Is there some kind of problem?
- What problem?

712
00:48:43,024 --> 00:48:44,609
Let's say they're moral support.

713
00:48:44,692 --> 00:48:48,196
Well then, the goods are checked.

714
00:48:48,279 --> 00:48:49,989
And you've got your moral support.

715
00:48:50,281 --> 00:48:52,325
Please sign the delivery receipt.

716
00:48:58,498 --> 00:48:59,499
Good work.

717
00:48:59,582 --> 00:49:01,918
We got paid and the delivery went well.
It's a win-win.

718
00:49:02,001 --> 00:49:04,587
I'll let the guys in mainland know
that the deal went smoothly.

719
00:49:06,881 --> 00:49:08,675
I've been waiting for this day.

720
00:49:09,676 --> 00:49:11,010
Ah, what a beauty.

721
00:49:11,886 --> 00:49:13,846
Hey, let's grab it and get out of here.

722
00:49:13,930 --> 00:49:16,391
- Let's not waste time. Got it?
- Yes, sir.

723
00:49:18,977 --> 00:49:20,478
Hey, Kim. Bring it down.

724
00:49:21,646 --> 00:49:22,855
Yes, sir.

725
00:49:33,491 --> 00:49:36,286
We're all set here.
It's time to have some fun.

726
00:49:41,624 --> 00:49:42,625
What the hell?

727
00:49:44,335 --> 00:49:45,336
Go check that out.

728
00:49:46,462 --> 00:49:47,630
Kim, I said pull it down.

729
00:49:50,717 --> 00:49:52,427
Didn't you hear me? Get it down!

730
00:49:55,638 --> 00:49:56,681
Mr. Yoo?

731
00:49:58,224 --> 00:50:00,101
What's going on here?

732
00:50:03,396 --> 00:50:06,065
This is well within my expectations.
No need to panic.

733
00:50:08,484 --> 00:50:10,403
What are you waiting for?
Did you forget Plan B?

734
00:50:13,823 --> 00:50:16,534
All right, kids, get ready for Plan B.

735
00:50:16,618 --> 00:50:17,619
Let's go!

736
00:50:18,536 --> 00:50:19,829
- Focus. Get ready.
- Yeah.

737
00:50:24,709 --> 00:50:25,877
Damn it, what is that?

738
00:50:28,880 --> 00:50:30,006
Come on, kids.

739
00:50:30,089 --> 00:50:33,384
You should be holding pencils,
not weapons.

740
00:50:35,887 --> 00:50:37,680
Focus!

741
00:50:39,140 --> 00:50:40,475
- Go!
- Let's go!

742
00:50:43,019 --> 00:50:44,896
What the hell?

743
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:47,565
Hey, are we supposed to jump?

744
00:50:50,068 --> 00:50:51,986
- Everyone get ready.
- Yes, sir.

745
00:50:52,070 --> 00:50:54,280
Boys!

746
00:51:00,161 --> 00:51:01,245
Look, Boss!

747
00:51:05,500 --> 00:51:07,168
Martial Arts Master.

748
00:51:07,251 --> 00:51:09,379
I was wondering when you'd show up.

749
00:51:09,462 --> 00:51:11,714
- Two of you this time.
- How many times do I have to say it?

750
00:51:12,465 --> 00:51:16,761
I said it's Masked Racer. Masked Racer!

751
00:51:18,179 --> 00:51:19,889
That masked freak is back.

752
00:51:20,640 --> 00:51:22,684
Whatever you are,
why do you keep showing up

753
00:51:22,767 --> 00:51:24,394
and messing with my business?

754
00:51:24,477 --> 00:51:29,023
Masked Racer keeps appearing
because you keep doing bad things.

755
00:51:29,857 --> 00:51:30,858
But today?

756
00:51:31,275 --> 00:51:34,696
I didn't come to mess with you.
I came to see the first snow.

757
00:51:36,572 --> 00:51:38,157
What is he on about?

758
00:51:40,910 --> 00:51:45,540
You think I'd just nod my head
and let you get away?

759
00:51:46,749 --> 00:51:49,961
I knew you'd be here,
so I already dug your grave, you bastard.

760
00:51:50,795 --> 00:51:53,423
You can't just rely on numbers
to win a fight.

761
00:51:53,506 --> 00:51:55,383
You have to use your head.

762
00:51:56,592 --> 00:51:59,929
Well, we've finally gathered
all of you good people in one place.

763
00:52:00,847 --> 00:52:02,265
So what do you say?

764
00:52:02,849 --> 00:52:04,726
Shall we watch the first snow together?

765
00:52:32,044 --> 00:52:33,171
What's wrong with this thing?

766
00:52:34,380 --> 00:52:35,923
Hey, you gotta press it harder.

767
00:52:40,887 --> 00:52:41,888
That's not it.

768
00:52:45,183 --> 00:52:46,601
Dude, it's not working.

769
00:52:46,684 --> 00:52:48,311
Crap, could it have gotten too old?

770
00:52:48,394 --> 00:52:51,189
Hey, Ho-myeong, press it harder.
Really push it.

771
00:52:52,732 --> 00:52:55,359
Just press it harder, you idiot!

772
00:52:57,653 --> 00:52:59,155
Damn it, it's not working!

773
00:52:59,655 --> 00:53:00,782
Is this thing broken?

774
00:53:00,865 --> 00:53:02,408
- What the hell?
- Damn it.

775
00:53:05,661 --> 00:53:07,914
- Press it harder.
- What the hell are they doing?

776
00:53:08,915 --> 00:53:10,833
Find out how that bastard
climbed up there.

777
00:53:12,126 --> 00:53:13,252
Oh, come on!

778
00:53:15,630 --> 00:53:16,631
Damn it!

779
00:53:59,048 --> 00:54:00,049
Damn it!

780
00:54:03,511 --> 00:54:04,679
- No!
- No.

781
00:54:04,762 --> 00:54:06,347
Get all those guys!

782
00:56:36,580 --> 00:56:38,165
I'll kill those bastards!

783
00:56:39,250 --> 00:56:41,085
Hey, bring me the nephew.

784
00:56:52,096 --> 00:56:55,224
- What are you doing here?
- Wasn't there a gunshot just now?

785
00:56:55,558 --> 00:56:57,601
You have no idea
how dangerous those guys are.

786
00:56:58,728 --> 00:57:00,479
- Stay perfectly still.
- Okay.

787
00:57:05,693 --> 00:57:08,070
- Did you get enough evidence?
- I am right now.

788
00:57:08,904 --> 00:57:10,614
This is a crucial moment.

789
00:57:14,744 --> 00:57:15,745
Stop!

790
00:57:16,954 --> 00:57:19,248
Stop unless you want to
watch this kid die!

791
00:57:19,790 --> 00:57:20,791
Nam-il.

792
00:57:21,083 --> 00:57:22,084
What did you say?

793
00:57:22,418 --> 00:57:23,669
My nephew, Nam-il.

794
00:57:24,253 --> 00:57:25,254
What's he doing there?

795
00:57:26,505 --> 00:57:28,215
What are you doing? Are you crazy?

796
00:57:28,340 --> 00:57:30,676
I have to save him.
He could die if he stays there.

797
00:57:30,760 --> 00:57:33,512
But what can you do? Do you have a plan?

798
00:57:33,596 --> 00:57:35,848
- Just wait. I'll radio it in.
- No.

799
00:57:35,931 --> 00:57:37,099
There's no time for that.

800
00:57:40,603 --> 00:57:42,730
Oh my god. What are you doing?

801
00:57:47,318 --> 00:57:50,446
Ms. Gang, please hit me in the head
with this as hard as you can.

802
00:57:50,529 --> 00:57:52,198
Are you insane?

803
00:57:55,367 --> 00:57:56,786
I have a plan.

804
00:57:57,453 --> 00:57:59,246
Just trust me.

805
00:57:59,330 --> 00:58:02,374
Hit me in the head as hard as you can.

806
00:58:02,500 --> 00:58:03,501
I'm begging you.

807
00:58:04,710 --> 00:58:05,711
Please.

808
00:58:05,795 --> 00:58:08,714
Hurry.

809
00:58:08,798 --> 00:58:10,925
Nam-il is going to die at this rate!

810
00:58:13,177 --> 00:58:14,178
Oh my god!

811
00:58:15,346 --> 00:58:16,388
Je-sun.

812
00:58:17,890 --> 00:58:19,433
This is crazy.

813
00:58:22,853 --> 00:58:25,272
Mi-kyung, bring the car here.
It's an emergency.

814
00:58:29,276 --> 00:58:30,277
Damn it.

815
00:58:30,361 --> 00:58:32,530
Go ahead if you want your nephew to die.

816
00:58:33,280 --> 00:58:34,740
Nephew? What nephew?

817
00:58:34,824 --> 00:58:35,866
Hey, you have a nephew?

818
00:58:35,991 --> 00:58:37,118
I don't have a nephew.

819
00:58:42,289 --> 00:58:43,999
Wait a minute. That kid.

820
00:58:44,959 --> 00:58:46,001
Isn't he Bulgae's nephew?

821
00:58:46,502 --> 00:58:47,837
Hey, don't do it!

822
00:58:47,920 --> 00:58:49,421
He's not one of us.

823
00:58:49,505 --> 00:58:52,758
You think I'll believe that?
I'm gonna slit his throat.

824
00:58:53,509 --> 00:58:55,511
- What the hell?
- Get those bastards!

825
00:59:27,042 --> 00:59:28,752
One...

826
00:59:30,171 --> 00:59:31,755
Two...

827
00:59:43,642 --> 00:59:45,144
Uncle!

828
01:00:14,089 --> 01:00:15,633
Screw you, scumbag gangsters!

829
01:00:17,635 --> 01:00:20,846
Come on! I dare you!
I'm Heo Nam-il! Got it?

830
01:00:20,930 --> 01:00:24,141
I'm not going down alone. I'll throw it!
I swear I'll throw it!

831
01:00:32,650 --> 01:00:34,944
- What happened?
- Step on it. Head that way.

832
01:00:35,027 --> 01:00:37,029
- Where's Bong?
- Over there.

833
01:00:52,586 --> 01:00:54,922
- Get in, quick!
- Hurry!

834
01:01:02,513 --> 01:01:03,514
We got it!

835
01:01:08,143 --> 01:01:09,144
Wake up!

836
01:01:09,895 --> 01:01:11,021
Is he hurt badly?

837
01:01:11,313 --> 01:01:13,107
I don't know.
I don't see any external injuries.

838
01:01:14,608 --> 01:01:17,319
- His breathing's normal too.
- He turned into the Hulk.

839
01:01:17,403 --> 01:01:18,487
The Hulk?

840
01:01:19,446 --> 01:01:20,990
He'll be fine in a little bit.

841
01:01:22,366 --> 01:01:23,826
My uncle's no ordinary person.

842
01:01:23,909 --> 01:01:26,620
Forget about that!
Why was he on the ground over there?

843
01:01:27,037 --> 01:01:28,330
Ah, Prosecutor Gang!

844
01:01:28,414 --> 01:01:30,666
You got the video you wanted, right?

845
01:01:31,000 --> 01:01:33,252
I did, but there were some complications.

846
01:01:33,335 --> 01:01:36,213
- Complications?
- Let's just get back. I'll tell you then.

847
01:01:48,934 --> 01:01:51,061
- Should we go?
- Yeah. You okay?

848
01:01:51,145 --> 01:01:52,146
Yeah.

849
01:01:53,647 --> 01:01:54,648
What is it?

850
01:01:56,233 --> 01:01:57,234
I recognize that car.

851
01:01:57,318 --> 01:02:00,070
- Whatever. Just go.
- Okay.

852
01:02:10,039 --> 01:02:12,124
- We're done here. Let's get out.
- Huh?

853
01:02:12,666 --> 01:02:13,834
- Hey, it's time.
- Let's go!

854
01:02:24,386 --> 01:02:26,430
Hey, Boss, wake up already!

855
01:02:28,766 --> 01:02:30,642
Go after them, you idiots!

856
01:02:32,436 --> 01:02:33,979
Those bastards! Damn it!

857
01:02:43,489 --> 01:02:45,157
Unbelievable.

858
01:02:46,784 --> 01:02:47,785
Let's go.

859
01:02:51,163 --> 01:02:53,791
- Go after them!
- What's wrong with this thing?

860
01:02:53,874 --> 01:02:56,043
- What now?
- Something's wrong with the car.

861
01:02:56,126 --> 01:02:58,128
- Why isn't it working?
- Damn it!

862
01:03:00,923 --> 01:03:02,299
YEONGSEON FOOD

863
01:03:09,014 --> 01:03:10,015
Hurry up, you idiot!

864
01:03:11,934 --> 01:03:12,935
Come on!

865
01:03:21,026 --> 01:03:22,736
Yeah!

866
01:03:27,908 --> 01:03:29,701
That was freaking rough!

867
01:03:41,797 --> 01:03:44,425
SPECIAL THANKS TO
KIM SANG-KYUNG AND KWON YUL

868
01:03:59,231 --> 01:04:02,568
So these so-called Masked Racers
suddenly appeared out of nowhere

869
01:04:02,693 --> 01:04:04,486
and blew up all the drugs?

870
01:04:04,570 --> 01:04:06,697
- Hey, Boss!
- A double agent?

871
01:04:06,780 --> 01:04:09,658
- You sure you can handle this?
- Patrolling is my specialty. Don't worry.

872
01:04:09,741 --> 01:04:12,202
Honestly, she seemed
very suspicious to me.

873
01:04:12,327 --> 01:04:14,455
So she approached
Gang Beom-ryong on purpose?

874
01:04:14,538 --> 01:04:15,873
I'll watch him closely.

875
01:04:15,956 --> 01:04:18,208
You think I'm stupid enough
to let something like this break me?

876
01:04:20,127 --> 01:04:21,670
Je-sun. I'm just asking.

877
01:04:21,753 --> 01:04:24,715
What would you do if your past self
was a completely different person?

878
01:04:24,798 --> 01:04:26,341
You turned into the Hulk yesterday.

879
01:04:26,425 --> 01:04:27,676
Jeong Ho-myeong and I

880
01:04:27,759 --> 01:04:29,303
could be back at each other's throats
at any moment.

881
01:04:29,386 --> 01:04:32,055
- You bastard.
- You're the only one I can count on.

882
01:04:32,181 --> 01:04:35,601
- It's not too late for you to pull out.
- Is this a threat?

883
01:04:35,684 --> 01:04:38,312
- Gather all of our boys.
- You have to take responsibility.

884
01:04:38,395 --> 01:04:40,898
- I'm already prepared.
- Where the hell did Bulgae come from?

885
01:04:41,023 --> 01:04:43,901
- It was Je-sun.
- This is no coincidence.

886
01:04:43,984 --> 01:04:45,444
Change of plans.

